<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 2.30 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT RISES 2.30 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian banks' internal credit</p>
<p>rose to 1,125.6 billion levs on August 23 from 1,117.6 billion</p>
<p>levs a week earlier, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Credit to the government rose 1.55 percent to 472.3 billion</p>
<p>levs, credit to state firms increased 2.66 percent to 300.6</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms rose</p>
<p>4.43 percent to 132.1 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	     AUG 23-AUG 16   AUG 23-JULY 26</p>
<p> Total internal credit	    +2.30	     +3.45</p>
<p> Credit to govt		     +1.55	     +2.72</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	    +2.66	     +5.07</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms    +4.43	     +3.53</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	   AUG 23	 AUG 16    JULY 26</p>
<p> Total internal credit	   1,125.6     1,117.6    1,088.1</p>
<p> Credit to govt			472.3	 465.1	459.8</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	     300.6	 292.8	286.1</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms     132.1	 126.5	125.1</p>
<p>Dlr credit to private firms</p>
<p> (USD billion)			  $1.13	$1.13	  $1.16</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
